          "title": "跨越边界以后，为什么还必须形成下一尺度",
          "summary": "跨越旧边界只是扩展的开始。新节点必须形成可重复的资源循环、局部能力、制度化与修复机制，扩展才会稳定成新的正常尺度；而成熟运行最终还可能从“更大的自己”转变为更高尺度中的稳定节点。",
          "href": "/articles/book4-article-013",
          "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-013-ZH-HANS-ARTICLE"
        },
        {
          "locale": "en",
          "title": "Why Crossing a Boundary Still Requires a New Stable Scale",
          "summary": "Crossing an old boundary is only the beginning of expansion. New nodes must develop repeatable resource cycles, local capability, institutional continuity, and repair mechanisms before expansion becomes a stable new scale; a mature runtime may then stop trying to become a larger version of itself and instead become a stable node inside a higher-scale runtime.",
          "href": "/articles/book4-article-013",
          "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-013-EN-ARTICLE"
        }
      ],
      "summaryScope": "PUBLISHED_ARTICLE_SUMMARY_NOT_NEW_CANONICAL_DEFINITION",
