      "articles": [
        {
          "locale": "zh-Hans",
          "title": "当运行跨越人类与人工载体，接口为什么必须迁移",
          "summary": "当运行从生命、组织进一步跨入人工载体，真正改变的不是“机器做了多少”，而是现实首先被谁读取、压缩、判断与执行。接口迁移会把人类从部分重复与信息处理中移开，让人工系统进入知识、协调与执行层；跨载体扩展则要求生命、制度与人工结构保持可追溯、可替代、可修正的连接。下一尺度因此依赖的不是单一载体胜出，而是接口能否随着复杂度重新分配。",
          "href": "/articles/book4-article-034",
          "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-034-ZH-HANS-ARTICLE"
        },
        {
          "locale": "en",
          "title": "Why Interfaces Must Migrate When Runtime Crosses Human and Artificial Carriers",
          "summary": "When a runtime expands from life and organization into artificial carriers, the deepest change is not how much machines do, but who first reads, compresses, judges, and executes reality. Interface migration moves people away from some repetitive and information-heavy positions while artificial systems enter knowledge, coordination, and execution layers. Cross-carrier expansion therefore depends on traceable, replaceable, and revisable connections among life, institutions, organizations, and artificial structures.",
          "href": "/articles/book4-article-034",
          "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-034-EN-ARTICLE"
        }
      ],
      "summaryScope": "PUBLISHED_ARTICLE_SUMMARY_NOT_NEW_CANONICAL_DEFINITION",
      "humanAcceptanceComplete": false
    },
