          "locale": "zh-Hans",
          "title": "真正的扩展能力为什么取决于适应与结构投入",
          "summary": "长期扩展能力并不取决于系统已经拥有多少资源、技术与节点，而取决于它能否在旧方法接近边界时重新安排目标、载体、协调、资源与知识。与此同时，每一次更大尺度都必须支付结构成本，把原本隐性的关系转化成角色、制度、接口、技术、信息、冗余与维护；适应能力与结构投入共同决定扩展能否真正成立。",
          "href": "/articles/book4-article-025",
          "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-025-ZH-HANS-ARTICLE"
        },
        {
          "locale": "en",
          "title": "Why Real Expansion Capacity Depends on Adaptation and Structural Investment",
          "summary": "Long-term expansion does not depend on how many resources, technologies, and nodes a system already possesses, but on whether it can rearrange goals, carriers, coordination, resources, and knowledge when old methods approach their limits. Every larger scale also carries structural costs: tacit relationships must become roles, institutions, interfaces, technology, information systems, redundancy, and maintenance. Adaptation and structural investment together determine whether expansion can actually hold.",
          "href": "/articles/book4-article-025",
          "articleCode": "BOOK4-B4-ART-025-EN-ARTICLE"
        }
      ],
